regress/gate_hygiene.sh:365:#
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:366:#  (The `! -path artifacts' exclusion is load-bearing: the artifacts tree holds
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:367:#  FROZEN probe copies, which are evidence rather than gate material.)
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:368:#  *** RAISED 44 -> 46 BY pcc2widthkills, IN THE SAME COMMIT THAT ADDS THE TWO FILES --
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:369:#  pcc2_width_witness.py and pcc2_width_probe.py, both pty.fork, both promptless (fixed
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:370:#  timeouts, no endswith( predicate).  Written into the checkpoint at the moment the
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:371:#  witness was created, because #500 added a probe and moved NEITHER census, and it took
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:372:#  two passes and three seats to find. ***
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:373:#  *** 46 -> 73 ON 2026-09-23 BY ONE BULK RE-DERIVATION, BY OWNER RULING (hygienecensus; ledger row
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:374:#  stateaudit0923).  The pin had sat at 46 since b78bb0f (2026-09-03) while committed pty probes grew to
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:375:#  70, so this gate was RED AT HEAD -- measured on a pure export of HEAD's regress/, not inferred.  73 =
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:376:#  those 70 plus THREE UNTRACKED probes that lie in the tree and are counted as they sit, because the
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:377:#  census counts files, not commits: crime_width_probe.py (#529), arm_msrmode_probe.py (armmsrmodekill)
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:378:#  and lca_isaphys_probe.py (#540).  The owner chose to count all three in this denominator (2026-09-23,
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:379:#  "count all"); grandfathering crime_width_probe.py as PROMPTLESS is the part the ruling did not name -- it was
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:380:#  reported to the owner as a third name, not assumed authorised.  Consequence, stated so nobody
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:381:#  meets it cold: until all three are committed, a FRESH CLONE counts FEWER than 73 (70 with none of them)
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:382:#  and reds THREE rows -- this one, the promptless count and the promptless-names row -- because all three are
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:383:#  grandfathered names that exist only in the working tree (measured on a copy with them removed: 70/73, 40/43,
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:384:#  names gone=the three).  Written by `tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh --write`, never by hand. ***
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:385:EXPECT_PTY_PROBES=74
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:386:#  *** AND THE SAME PROBE BROKE A SECOND CENSUS IN THIS FILE, WHICH pass 11's OWN
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:387:#  REPAIR DID NOT FIX.  Found by the codex seat reviewing that repair. ***
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:388:#
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:389:#  `#500' added `sgi_de_primop_probe.py', and it broke BOTH pty censuses here:
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:427:#  alpha_tbi_probe.py has a real readiness wait the census cannot see (`"gxemul>" in buf[...].lower()`).
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:428:#  GRANDFATHERED, not converted:
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:429:#  converting a probe's readiness is its own round.  The block beginning `arm_msrmode_probe.py`
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:430:#  (2026-09-23, OWNER RULING): arm_msrmode_probe.py (armmsrmodekill) and lca_isaphys_probe.py (#540).  The
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:431:#  block beginning `crime_width_probe.py` (2026-09-23, pass 2 of this round, under the same ruling's
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:432:#  principle): crime_width_probe.py (#529), hidden from this census by a comment until pass 2 stopped the
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:433:#  classifier reading full-line comments (it reads tokens since the F2 repair).  All three are UNTRACKED and lying
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:434:#  in the tree, named so the census passes on
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:435:#  the tree the weekly battery runs.  Re-derive, never hand-edit: `bash tools/derive_hygiene_pins.sh` (report),
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:436:#  `--grandfather NAME...` / `--release NAME...`, then `--write`.
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:437:
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:438:#  *** THIS WAS THE THIRD POPULATION AND THE F2 EDIT MISSED IT.  Found by the agy seat
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:439:#  on pass 2. ***  py_code and probe_code were converted to recursive-minus-artifacts
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:440:#  while this line kept a FLAT GLOB -- so two censuses were aligned and a third was not,
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:441:#  which is the exact defect F2 exists to end.
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:442:#
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:443:#  It AGREES today (recursive-minus-artifacts == flat == 59) and that agreement is a
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:444:#  COINCIDENCE, not a property: a .py added in any NEW non-artifacts subdirectory would
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:445:#  be scanned by two censuses and missed by this one.  Equal counts are not an aligned
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:446:#  population, and reading the equality as safety is how the flat glob survived the
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:447:#  first repair.
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:448:#  hygienecensus F2: paths RELATIVE TO regress/, not basenames -- a probe in a subdirectory was classified by a
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:449:#  same-named top-level file (measured: a promptless copy at newsub/ read as prompt-detecting), and a bare xargs
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:450:#  split a filename holding a space.  NUL-safe as far as grep: `grep -l` prints one name per LINE, so a file name
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:451:#  holding a newline is not supported (and a name holding a space cannot be grandfathered -- the list is
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:452:#  space-separated; the deriver refuses it by name).  For every file in regress/ itself the relative path IS the basename, so the
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:453:#  grandfathered names are unchanged.
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:454:_ptylist=$(find "$HERE" -name "*.py" -type f ! -path "$HERE/artifacts/*" -print0 2>/dev/null \
