regress/gate_hygiene.sh:462:#  n2a, n2b, n9).  A comment, a string or a docstring is never a "." NAME "(" sequence of tokens, so none of
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:463:#  those can hide a probe now; and the classifier keeps STATEMENT boundaries, so a method reference on one line
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:464:#  and a parenthesised string on the next is not a call (the closing pass, codex -- controls_c2/t_nljoin).  A file that cannot be read or tokenized is listed promptless (it cannot
regress/gate_hygiene.sh:465:#  be read, so it is not trusted).  The spelling counts above deliberately stay textual, so a comment or a string
